# Complete routing245 coverage publication design

This is an unexecuted packet-builder implementation for an explicitly pinned routing245 coverage manifest and guard. It does not assert complete coverage. The first fixed-v3 proposal is preserved under `history/fixed-v3-unexecuted/`; a later cut49 failure made its fixed census unsuitable. The active builder derives counts from the supplied reviewed manifest and requires an independent complete receipt for every selected module. No refinement is accepted by name or directory alone.

## Fixed family and release gate

Require command-line paths and exact SHA values for the selected manifest and actual guard. The manifest supplies new/reused module descriptors and probe/caller counts; independently recompute both totals, validate unique module names, and compare them with the future complete-review receipt. Recompute the final import closure from actual source imports and provider pairs and require the independent receipt to agree. The routed245 tree remains fixed at 6,460 leaves, 8,391 guards and depth 51. The three exact historical pilot record hashes remain a fixed whitelist; every other reused unit is a normal production proof. V3 had 209 new and 17 reused modules (476/479), but those numbers are now historical and are not active release gates.

The builder accepts a final complete batch descriptor and its exact SHA, plus an independent final evidence receipt and its exact SHA. It recursively resolves the batch's explicit `prior_batches`, validates their manifest pins, and merges completed-unit records by module. Conflicting descriptors for one module are rejected. A failed earlier batch may contribute its actual completed successes; its failed record must remain separate. A successful selected-range batch is insufficient by itself. Require a terminal `PASS_COMPLETE_COVERAGE` batch, every unique new-unit PASS record, every exact reused record from the manifest, and the final `SitesRouting245` record. Require all selected source/audit identities to match the frozen family and the final receipt's complete module-to-record index.

For every selected record, independently check PASS/non-prepare status, successful ordered source/audit commands, shared 120-second budget, `-j1 -M4096`, default proof limits, zero recorded and raw warnings, actual standard-axiom reports in exact audit order, caller census, source/audit snapshots, before/after identity, current input hashes, actual first providers, exact import DFS, and the fresh object saved before the audit and unchanged afterward. Three historical pilot records lack the later `preparation` field: allow that exception only for the three exact manifest-pinned pilot records and document it. Every production record, including reused v1 batches and cut43, must have its exact original `PREPARED_NOT_BUILT` receipt with no commands/fresh objects and correct inputs/providers. Do not synthesize missing historical fields.

Recompute the final project-provider import closure from the selected source graph. Compare each selected ancestor's source/object pair to the provider pair used by the final proof. This binds both children of cut42 and every reused module to the actual final theorem. Require all current input hashes to remain identical after packet staging.

